%% One voice turn: same graph, same authorization as text; sentences are spoken as soon as they pass the guard
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Applicant (browser /voice)
    participant LK as LiveKit 1.13 :7880
    participant W as Voice worker<br/>(LiveKit Agents 1.8)
    participant STT as Gnani Prisma v3.0 STT
    participant S as Server :8095
    participant G as Graph + SentenceGate<br/>(inside the server)
    participant TTS as Gnani Timbre v3.0 TTS

    A->>S: POST /api/session, then /api/livekit-token
    S-->>A: LiveKit JWT (metadata carries the advisory session token)
    A->>LK: join room, publish mic
    LK->>W: audio frames
    W->>W: Silero VAD: end of speech
    W->>STT: streamed PCM (language from the session locale)
    STT-->>W: transcript
    W->>S: POST /api/chat/stream, channel = voice<br/>Authorization: Bearer session token
    S->>G: run graph (voice deadline AGENT_VOICE_DEADLINE_S, default 25 s)
    opt English explain / improve
        G-->>W: lead sentence built from recorded ZEN evidence (no LLM)
    end
    loop each sentence of the LLM draft
        G->>G: same deterministic guards on the sentence
        alt sentence passes
            G-->>W: {"type":"sentence"}
            W->>TTS: POST /api/v1/tts/sse (voice Tarika, speed)
            TTS-->>W: PCM chunks as they arrive
            W->>LK: agent audio track
            LK-->>A: spoken sentence
        else sentence flagged
            G->>G: stop streaming - full validate → rewrite or template
        end
    end
    opt nothing guarded yet after VOICE_FILLER_AFTER_S (4 s)
        W->>TTS: "One moment, please." (localized)
    end
    G-->>W: {"type":"final", response} (remainder after a short bridge if a draft was replaced)
    W->>LK: answer card on data channel (topic "advisor")
    LK-->>A: decision card + citations
    Note over W,S: worker HTTP timeout 40 s > graph deadline, so the graph's own fallback answers first,<br/>if the server is unreachable the worker speaks a localized apology
